# A relative path naming a file that does not exist cannot be resolved
# through real_path (which needs the file on disk), so canonicalization
# falls back to making it absolute against the working directory.
#
# For a Replacement, the missing file's edit is dropped and the diagnostic
# names the spelling as the input gave it — what the producer wrote and the
# only string the reader can search their YAML for — so the make_absolute
# fallback is not observable through FilePath. It is observable through
# MainSourceFile, which is never existence-checked: both inputs name a main
# source file that does not exist, by the same relative spelling, and the
# merged document carries its absolute form.

# RUN: rm -rf %t.dir
# RUN: mkdir -p %t.dir
# RUN: printf '%%80s' '' > %t.dir/foo.cpp

# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/non-overlapping-a.tpl.yaml %t.dir/a.yaml
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/single-replacement.tpl.yaml %t.dir/b.yaml
# (One -e per sed: under lit, BSD sed binds -i's suffix to the next word.)
# RUN: sed -i'' -e "s|MainSourceFile:  '@FOO@'|MainSourceFile:  'nope/missing.c'|; s|@FOO@|nope/missing.cpp|g" %t.dir/a.yaml
# RUN: sed -i'' -e "s|MainSourceFile:  '@FOO@'|MainSourceFile:  'nope/missing.c'|; s|@FOO@|%/t.dir/foo.cpp|g" %t.dir/b.yaml

# RUN: cd %t.dir && clang-ssaf-src-edit-merge -o %t.dir/merged.yaml \
# RUN:     %t.dir/a.yaml %t.dir/b.yaml 2> %t.dir/stderr.txt

# The diagnostic names the raw spelling.
# RUN: FileCheck --input-file=%t.dir/stderr.txt --check-prefix=STDERR %s
# STDERR:     clang-ssaf-src-edit-merge: nope/missing.cpp: file does not exist; skipping its replacement(s)
# STDERR-NOT: {{.}}

# foo.cpp's edit is untouched. What pins "the missing file's edit is gone"
# is the `...` terminator directly after the one surviving entry — a second
# entry would land between them and break the CHECK-NEXT chain. Path
# literals assume a symlink-free %t; see canonical-path-dedup.test.
# RUN: FileCheck --input-file=%t.dir/merged.yaml -DDIR=%/t.dir %s
# CHECK:      MainSourceFile:  '[[DIR]]/nope/missing.c'
# CHECK-NEXT: Replacements:
# CHECK-NEXT:   - FilePath:        '[[DIR]]/foo.cpp'
# CHECK-NEXT:     Offset:          10
# CHECK-NEXT:     Length:          3
# CHECK-NEXT:     ReplacementText: X
# CHECK-NEXT: ...
